          "date": "2026-10-30 00:02:12.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-06 02:14:25.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity-quota test_3a and test_3b",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: shorten sanity-quota test_3a and test_3b\n\ntest_3a and test_3b each run test_block_soft() for the user,\ngroup and project quota types. Every cycle waits out the block\ngrace time (20s on ldiskfs, 60s on ZFS, plus 5s) and runs\nseveral wait_delete_completed and syncs, so each test spends\nabout 50s per quota type on ldiskfs and about 125s on ZFS.\n\nRun the group type only with SLOW=yes. User and project quotas\nstill run by default, and the group quota code shares the same\nsoft limit and grace handling.\n\nOn a rocky9 ldiskfs test VM, ONLY=\"3a 3b\" took 146s and 147s\nfor test_3a, 153s and 154s for test_3b before, and 99s and 102s\nfor test_3a, 106s and 107s for test_3b after; with SLOW=yes the\ntimes are unchanged (149s and 154s). Expected CI saving, using\nCI means of 322s (3a) and 336s (3b) over about 7100 runs each\nper 30 days and about 47s per run on ldiskfs (measured) and\nabout 123s per run on ZFS (estimated, about 3700 runs): roughly\n340 hours per 30 days across both tests.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=\"3a 3b\"\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ia71ed2f82466c1214f8ee1bfc086a7182aafe3e9\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/70196\nReviewed-by: Sergey Cheremencev <scherementsev@ddn.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
